THIS PROJECT IS TO BE ABLE TO VISUALIZE GRAPHICALLY MATRIXES AND THEIR OPERATIONS

Tkinter	Buttons, inputs, windows	Start here
NumPy	Matrix calculations	Use for checking your results
Matplotlib	Graphs, vectors, coordinate grids	Add later
Pygame	Custom interactive graphics and animation	Optional advanced stage
SymPy	Symbolic calculations and exact algebra	Optional later



 1. Set up your project
[X] Create a main.py file
[ ] Learn basic Git usage 

2. Learn Python fundamentals
[ ] Learn imports and modules
[ ] Handle invalid input with exceptions
[X] Learn basic classes and objects

3. Implement matrix basics
[X] Represent matrices as nested lists
[ ] Validate matrix dimensions and rectangular shape
[X] Create a function to display a matrix in the terminal
[X] Implement matrix addition
[X] Implement matrix subtraction
[ ] Implement scalar multiplication
[X] Implement matrix transpose
[X] Implement matrix multiplication
[ ] Test incompatible dimensions and edge cases

4. Implement linear algebra
[X] Calculate the determinant of a 2×2 matrix
[ ] Implement determinants for larger square matrices
[ ] Learn and implement Gaussian elimination
[ ] Implement matrix rank
[ ] Implement matrix inverse
[X] Detect singular matrices (determinant equals zero)
[X] Implement elementary row operations
[ ] Display intermediate calculation steps

5. Build the graphical interface
[ ] Learn basic Tkinter windows and widgets
[X] Create the main application window
[ ] Build a dynamic matrix input grid
[ ] Allow the user to change row and column counts
[ ] Add buttons for matrix operations
[ ] Display results in a readable format
[ ] Show helpful error messages
[ ] Separate GUI code from matrix calculations

6. Add visualizations
[ ] Learn Cartesian coordinates and 2D vectors
[X] Draw coordinate axes and a grid
[X] Draw the unit square and basis vectors
[ ] Apply a 2×2 matrix to points and vectors
[ ] Display the transformed square and vectors
[ ] Show the determinant and area scaling
[ ] Handle reflections and determinant-zero transformations
[X] Add zooming, panning, or animation if desired

7. Test and polish
[ ] Write unit tests for matrix operations
[ ] Test zero matrices, identity matrices, and negative values
[ ] Test singular and non-square matrices
[ ] Compare selected results against NumPy
[ ] Improve layout, labels, and keyboard navigation
[ ] Add example matrices and a reset button
[ ] Write a README explaining how to run the project
[ ] Package or share the finished application



